Section 13, and what it means here

AGPL differs from GPL in one clause that matters for a website: if you run a
modified version of this where other people can reach it over a network, those
people are entitled to its source. Not just people you distribute a copy to —
anyone who uses the running service.

That obligation binds us as much as anyone, which is why the footer of every
page links to this repository. If you fork this and put it online, your footer
has to point at yours.

You may use this commercially. That is not an oversight.

